#: includes/settings/views/ffc-tab-advanced.php:606
msgid "CPF/RF and e-mail are encrypted at rest using your WordPress secret keys (or the FFC decoupling constants). If those secrets are missing, weak, or still the wp-config sample placeholder, the encryption key and the search-hash salt become predictable — this panel reports their real state."
msgstr "O CPF/RF e o e-mail são criptografados em repouso utilizando as chaves secretas do seu WordPress (ou as constantes de desacoplamento do FFC). Se esses segredos estiverem ausentes, forem fracos ou ainda mantiverem os valores padrão do arquivo de exemplo `wp-config`, a chave de criptografia e o *salt* para o *hash* de busca tornam-se previsíveis — este painel informa a situação real deles."

#: includes/settings/views/documentation/config-advanced.php:42
msgid "CPF/RF and e-mail are encrypted at rest. By default FFC derives its encryption key and search-hash salt from your WordPress secret keys (SECURE_AUTH_KEY, LOGGED_IN_KEY, NONCE_KEY). This panel reports whether that secret material is strong, and lets you optionally decouple FFC from the WordPress salts."
msgstr "O CPF/RF e o e-mail são criptografados em repouso. Por padrão, o FFC deriva sua chave de criptografia e o *salt* para *hash* de busca a partir das chaves secretas do WordPress (SECURE_AUTH_KEY, LOGGED_IN_KEY, NONCE_KEY). Este painel informa se esses dados secretos são robustos e permite, opcionalmente, desvincular o FFC dos *salts* do WordPress."

